    "bounds": "A15 rival 2 only",
    "rival_2_as_restated_here": "the epithelial integrin's effect on the fibroblast may be indirect, mediated by a change in the epithelium rather than by TGF-beta activated at the epithelial surface acting on the fibroblast",
    "why_restated": "RATIONALE.md grounded rival 2 in Morris 2003 and Koth 2007 as non-TGF-beta routes, but both papers attribute their phenotypes to loss of TGF-beta activation in their own titles. A metalloproteinase and surfactant panel would therefore measure TGF-beta-mediated consequences of removing the integrin and would not separate rival 2 from the mechanism A15 proposes. The separable question is whether the epithelium changes at all.",
    "is_not": "a test of A15. This deposit fails A15 stage 1 gate conditions 1, 3, 4 and 5: no recorded validation that the perturbation took effect, no activated-TGF-beta readout, no separated fibroblast compartment, and no ligand arm.",
